.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt DTFL-SERVER 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl-server
.Nd shared-dataflow plugin server
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar session-file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the differential-dataflow
.Ql dd_server :
a long-running host for several dataflows
.Pq Dq plugins
that share arrangements by name.
One plugin publishes an indexed collection
.Pq a trace
under a name, and other plugins import that same trace into their own
dataflows, so the cost of indexing the collection is paid once and shared
across every importer.
.Pp
.Nm
reads a command session from
.Ar session-file ,
or standard input.
The four example plugins are linked in and selected by name; a line beginning
with
.Ql #
or
.Ql --
is a comment.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic load Ar instance plugin Op Ar args ...
Build
.Ar plugin Ap s
dataflow on the shared worker under the given
.Ar instance
name, passing the positional
.Ar args .
Several loads of one plugin under different instance names coexist, each its
own dataflow sharing the same imported traces.
.It Ic tick
Close the current epoch, advance every plugin input, and run to quiescence.
.It Ic drop Ar instance
Drop a loaded instance, releasing its dataflow and the inputs it created.
Traces it published stay registered for importers that still reference them.
.It Ic peek Ar trace
Print a registered trace's consolidated contents as of the current epoch.
Records are shown as a tuple of their fields.
.It Ic list
Print the registry: the epoch, each registered trace, each loaded instance.
.It Ic plugins
List the registered plugins.
.It Ic exit
Stop the session.
.El
.Pp
The host time is a
.Vt u64
epoch shared across all plugins, advanced by one each
.Ic tick .
.Ss Plugins
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic random_graph Ar name nodes edges rate
Generate a deterministic graph of
.Ar edges
random edges over
.Ar nodes
nodes, arrange it by source node, and publish the trace under
.Ar name .
The
.Ar rate
argument is accepted and ignored
.Pq see Sx STANDARDS .
.It Ic degr_dist Ar graph
Import the shared
.Ar graph
edge trace and compute its degree distribution, published under
.Ar graph Ns Fl degrees
as
.Pq Vt degree , Vt count
rows.
.It Ic reachability Ar graph source
Import the shared
.Ar graph
edge trace and compute the set of nodes reachable from
.Ar source ,
published under
.Ar graph Ns Fl reach .
.It Ic neighborhood Ar graph source
Import the shared
.Ar graph
edge trace and report the nodes reachable from
.Ar source
in exactly three hops.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${datadir}/dtfl/server/sessions/
The example sessions, replayable with
.Nm .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Generate a graph, then run two queries that share its arrangement:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
load graph random_graph graph 5 8 1000
load dd degr_dist graph
load rr reachability graph 0
tick
peek graph-degrees
peek graph-reach
exit
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl-ddir 1 ,
.Xr dtfl_collection_arrange_by_key 3
.Sh STANDARDS
Ported from the differential-dataflow
.Ql server
crate at tag
.Ql differential-dataflow-v0.25.1 .
Upstream loads plugins as dynamic libraries through
.Xr dlopen 3 ;
this port registers them statically
.Pq a name and a build callback ,
since library code may not
.Xr dlopen 3 .
The
.Ic random_graph
plugin upstream is an open-loop timed source;
this port produces only its deterministic initial graph, so a session is
replayable and its results are hand-checkable.
